      "ceterms:requires": [
        {
          "@type": "ceterms:ConditionProfile",
          "ceterms:name": {
            "en-US": "Requirements for Issuance"
          },
          "ceterms:condition": {
            "en-US": [
              "Possession of a baccalaureate degree or higher from a regionally-accredited college or university. If the degree major meets subject matter competence, the applicant does not qualify for the Provisional Internship Permit.",
              "Successful completion of course work for the permit type requested, as specified below:"
            ]
          },
          "ceterms:subjectWebpage": "https://www.ctc.ca.gov/credentials/leaflets/cl-856/"
        }
      ],
      "ceterms:renewal": [
        {
          "@type": "ceterms:ConditionProfile",
          "ceterms:name": {
            "en-US": "One-Time Renewal:"
          },
          "ceterms:condition": {
            "en-US": [
              "For a PIP initially issued before October 1, 2013, the employing agency may request a one-time only renewal if the holder has taken but not passed all the subject matter examinations or earned a degree major appropriate to the credential that authorizes the service listed on the permit. The holder of an Education Specialist PIP must take all appropriate subject matter examinations or earn a degree major as determined appropriate by the recommending college or university.",
              "The renewal packet, submitted through the employing agency, should include an application, a new Verification of Requirements for the Provisional Internship Permit (form CL-857) including all appropriate documentation, and current processing fee .",
              "If the holder has met subject matter competence, they should contact a California college or university or school district with a Commission-approved intern program regarding enrollment.",
              "Note [3]: The last date to submit an application for the Provisional Internship Permit in one of the Specialized Science content areas was January 1, 2015. The Provisional Internship Permit (only those initially issued prior to October 1, 2013) can no longer be reissued in one of these content areas."
            ]
          },
          "ceterms:subjectWebpage": "https://www.ctc.ca.gov/credentials/leaflets/cl-856/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ceterms:ConditionProfile",
          "ceterms:name": {
            "en-US": "Period of Validity:"
          },
          "ceterms:condition": {
            "en-US": [
              "The PIP will be issued for one year.",
              "Reference: Title 5, California Code of Regulations, Section 80021.1 CL-856 July 2022"
            ]
          },
          "ceterms:subjectWebpage": "https://www.ctc.ca.gov/credentials/leaflets/cl-856/"
        }
      ],
